euses an existing peer when one is in any non-terminal state (`!== 'closed' && !== 'error'`) so the athlete can reopen PairScreen mid-session without tearing down pairing, captures the local `onStateChange`/`onMessage` unsubscribes in refs so they detach cleanly on unmount or explicit Disconnect (regression fix for the reviewer's #1+#2 — without it, reopens stacked listeners and the reuse branch never re-bound them), and exposes a `Disconnect phone` button that calls `detachPhonePeer()`. `App.tsx` wires `onOpenPair` from IdleScreen and tracks a `pairOpener` state so closing PairScreen returns to whichever view opened it (Idle or Settings). Verify-script `app/verify-phase-2b4.mjs` runs C1–C4 gate-grade checks (option present + Idle banner + disabled Start + pair-now navigates + keyboard-default unaffected) and C5 best-effort (Disconnect button when peer connected — best-effort under §B2 because headless chromium without UDP cannot reach `connected`), plus M1–M7 manual checklist for operator sign-off. 10 new vitest tests (190 total, was 180; +9 phone-peer slice including the swap-broadcast regression for nit #8, +1 session inputSource='phone'). Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Bundle: main 345.86 KB / 107.01 KB gzip (Phase 2b.3 baseline 344.22 / 106.44 — +1.64 KB raw / +0.57 KB gzip for the slice + Idle/Trainer wiring); PairScreen chunk 140.63 KB / 51.21 KB gzip (+0.68 KB raw / +0.19 KB gzip for Disconnect + bindLocal helper); PhoneApp chunk unchanged. No bundle budget was specified for 2b.4 in the decision memo; the increase is the necessary cost of the new slice + Idle gate + Trainer subscription. Code-reviewer (`code-reviewer` agent) returned REQUEST-CHANGES with 0 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits; all five should-fixes were applied before approval (#1+#2 PairScreen listener leak + half-bound reuse FIXED via `bindLocal(peer, profile, sendArmedOnConnect)` shared helper + ref-tracked unsubscribes; #3 reuse predicate broadened to non-terminal states FIXED; #4 TrainerScreen phase-ref FIXED; #5 dispatch-commit DRY FIXED) plus three nits (#6 testids on Settings select + Save FIXED, #8 slice unwire-before-close ordering FIXED with regression test, #9 onCommit JSDoc clarification FIXED). Nit #7 (banner wording for transitional `phoneStatus` values) deferred — the message accurately reports the live PeerState and downstream phases can refine the copy if it surfaces as confusing in manual QA. Reviewer's optional `@testing-library/react`-based IdleScreen unit test deferred — adding the library is out of scope and the §B2 manual-QA + verify-script gating pattern (followed by 2b.1/2/3) covers the UI render path.",
  "decision_memo": "artifacts/decision-memo.md",
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "Settings input-source select offers 'Phone (motion)' alongside keyboard / pedal",
      "verified_by": "SettingsScreen.tsx renders three `<option>` elements including `<option value=\"phone\">Phone (motion)</option>` with `data-testid=\"input-source-select\"`. C1 in verify-phase-2b4.mjs PASS asserts the phone option exists with the right text. Backed by the union widening in engine/types.ts which makes 'phone' a typed-safe value passed through SettingsRecord.inputSource."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "If inputSource === 'phone' and no DataChannel is connected, Idle shows a 'Phone not paired — pair now' banner and disables Start",
      "verified_by": "IdleScreen.tsx subscribes to `usePhonePeer((s) => s.status)`; when `phoneSelected && !phoneReady` it renders the `data-testid=\"phone-not-paired\"` banner with a `pair now` button (`aria-label=\"pair phone now\"`) and computes `startDisabled = !profile || (phoneSelected && !phoneReady)`. C2 in verify-phase-2b4.mjs PASS asserts both — banner_count=1 and start_disabled=true. C3 PASS asserts the pair-now button navigates to PairScreen."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "With a paired phone, Start runs the drill and commits drive reps",
      "verified_by": "TrainerScreen's `dispatchCommit(at)` is invoked from both the keyboard handler and the `usePhonePeer.getState().onCommit(c => dispatchCommit(c.receivedAt))` subscription; both call `recordPress(at)` when phase is `waiting | showing`. The slice's `attachPhonePeer` mirrors the peer's state and fans out commit messages to subscribers — covered by phone-peer.test.ts 'fans out commit messages to onCommit subscribers' (would fail if the fan-out were reverted). End-to-end pair→drill flow is gated by M2+M3 manual QA per §B2 because headless chromium cannot complete a real WebRTC handshake."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Saved SessionRecord.inputSource === 'phone'",
      "verified_by": "session.test.ts 'accepts \\'phone\\' as an inputSource and stamps it on each rep' calls `start({...}, mulberry32(...), 'phone')` and asserts `rep.inputSource === 'phone'` + `state.inputSource === 'phone'`. session.ts:95 already passes `state.inputSource` into the persisted SessionRecord via `persistSession`. Widening the InputSource union was sufficient — no other code change needed. Manual M4 re-verifies the record makes it into the Recent sessions list + SummaryScreen with 'phone' label."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Existing 105+ tests still pass; new tests cover the union widening, IdleScreen pre-flight gate, TrainerScreen subscription path",
      "verified_by": "190/190 vitest tests pass (was 180 at Phase 2b.3 close; +10 new). Union widening covered by session.test.ts (+1 test). TrainerScreen subscription path covered structurally by phone-peer.test.ts 'fans out commit messages to onCommit subscribers' (the slice is the wire) + verified end-to-end manually under M3. IdleScreen pre-flight gate covered by verify-phase-2b4.mjs C2+C3 (banner appears + Start disabled + pair-now navigates) — a React-mounted IdleScreen unit test was deferred per §B2's UI-via-verify-script pattern, same approach used by 2b.1/2/3."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Manual real-device QA at app/verify-phase-2b4.mjs covers the full pair → calibrate → drill → summary flow with inputSource: 'phone'",
      "verified_by": "verify-phase-2b4.mjs writes M1–M7 manual_qa_checklist to artifacts/phase-2b4-verify/results.json: M1 (peer outlives PairScreen close), M2 (Start enables once paired), M3 (motion commits register as reps), M4 (SessionRecord.inputSource='phone' saved + visible in Recent sessions), M5 (channel-drop banner mid-drill), M6 (Idle pair-now → PairScreen → close returns to Idle), M7 (Settings → Pair → close returns to Settings). Current automated run: C1+C2+C3+C4 PASS (gate-grade), C5 FAIL (best-effort — Disconnect button under headless chromium can't reach 'connected'), console_errors=0."
    }
  ],
  "manual_qa": {
    "device_used": "not_performed_by_agent",
    "performed_by": "autonomous-agent",
    "performed_at": "2026-05-26",
    "playwright_run": {
      "automated_gate_checks": "C1, C2, C3, C4 PASS — Settings exposes the 'Phone (motion)' option; with inputSource='phone' and no peer the Idle banner renders + Start drill is disabled; the banner's 'pair now' button navigates to PairScreen; keyboard mode (default) has no banner and Start is enabled. Zero console errors across all four contexts.",
      "best_effort_disconnect_button": "C5 FAIL — the 'Disconnect phone' button only renders when peerState === 'connected', which headless chromium without UDP/STUN typically cannot reach. Same documented expected outcome as 2b.1's C5 and 2b.2's C2/C4 and 2b.3's C3 per QUALITY_GATES.md §'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b)' and the §B2 concession; manual M1 is the authoritative gate for the peer-outlives-view contract.",
      "console_errors": 0
    },
    "checklist_pending_operator_sign_off": [
      "M1 — Pair phone → connected → close PairScreen → phone-peer slice still reports connected (peer outlives view).",
      "M2 — With inputSource='phone' and peer connected, Idle's Start drill is enabled; click Start.",
      "M3 — Drill runs. Forward-snap impulses on phone register as reps in the trainer.",
      "M4 — Saved SessionRecord.inputSource === 'phone'; visible in SummaryScreen + IdleScreen 'Recent sessions' list.",
      "M5 — Disconnect phone mid-drill → TrainerScreen shows 'Phone disconnected' banner; no new commits register.",
      "M6 — IdleScreen 'pair now' → PairScreen → close returns to Idle (not Settings).",
      "M7 — Settings 'Pair phone' → PairScreen → close returns to Settings."
