    "operator_sign_off_instructions": "Update artifacts/phase-2b4-verify/results.json — set each entry's `signed_off` to {date:'YYYY-MM-DD', device:'<phone model + OS>'} after exercising the step on a real LAN+phone pair. The §B2 concession requires this field to be populated before the phase can be considered fully closed; the autonomous loop cannot perform real-device DataChannel + motion QA. M1+M2 prove the peer lifetime change (the architectural heart of 2b.4 per decision-memo §N5); M3+M4 prove the user-facing acceptance criterion 3+4; M5–M7 prove the user-flow ergonomics."
  },
  "gates": {
    "testing": "190/190 vitest tests pass (Phase 2b.3 baseline 180; +10 new). Every new public behavior in phone-peer.ts has a would-fail-if-reverted test: attach mirrors state, attach is idempotent on self, attach swaps the prior peer (closing it), detach is symmetric + idempotent + resets the slice, commit fanout reaches subscribers + drops non-commits + un-subscribes correctly, swap-broadcast regression for nit #8 (no spurious 'closed' status). Union widening covered by session.test.ts. UI flows (IdleScreen pre-flight, TrainerScreen subscription end-to-end with a real DataChannel) gated by manual real-device QA per the §B2 concession in QUALITY_GATES.md.",
    "dry": "phone-peer.ts is the single source of truth for the peer lifetime + status mirror + commit fanout; PairScreen, IdleScreen, TrainerScreen, and CalibrateScreen all consume the slice (via subscriptions or `getActivePhonePeer()`) rather than holding their own peer references. TrainerScreen's `dispatchCommit(at)` collapses the previously-duplicated keyboard and phone phase-routing into one helper. PairScreen's `bindLocal(peer, profile, sendArmedOnConnect)` collapses the previously-duplicated listener registration across the reuse and create branches.",
    "drift": "No prior-phase invariants touched. SessionRecord, RepRecord, ProfileRecord, Dexie schema version unchanged. Wire format unchanged from 2b.3. PhoneMessage union unchanged. The InputSource union widening is strictly additive (existing rows with 'keyboard'|'pedal' read back unchanged). PairScreen no longer closes the peer on unmount — a behavior change for prior phases' use cases (2b.1/2/3 closed on unmount) but justified by the §N5 resolution that the slice owns lifetime. Explicit Disconnect button preserves the closeability the prior behavior provided. CalibrateScreen still receives the peer via prop — unchanged — because PairScreen still has the peer ref. All 180 baseline tests still pass alongside the 10 new ones.",
