    "verification_sprint": "Pre-phase: re-ran lint + tsc + 180/180 tests + vite build at the Phase 2b.3 boundary before any 2b.4 code was added. Post-phase: 190/190 tests + lint + tsc + build all clean. Verify-phase-2b4.mjs C1–C4 PASS, C5 best-effort FAIL (documented).",
    "pre_commit_verify": "scripts/phasekit-verify.sh runs lint + typecheck + tests; all pass."
  },
  "review": {
    "architecture_red_team": "Cross-cutting concerns (B1 LAN trust, B2 testing-gate concession, B3 falsifiable motion criteria, B4 Android-gated acceptance) unchanged in this phase. The new architectural surface (phone-peer Zustand slice, peer-outlives-view lifetime, dispatch-commit DRY) is fully specified in decision-memo §N5 and was approved at the decomposition step. No new red-team risks introduced.",
    "code_reviewer": "REQUEST-CHANGES on the implementation. 0 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits. All five should-fix items APPLIED before approval: (#1+#2) PairScreen-local listener leak + half-bound reuse path FIXED with a shared `bindLocal(peer, profile, sendArmedOnConnect)` helper and ref-tracked `offStateRef`/`offMsgRef` unsubscribes that fire from both the unmount cleanup and the explicit Disconnect button; (#3) reuse predicate broadened from `state === 'connected'` to `state !== 'closed' && state !== 'error'` so in-flight handshakes survive PairScreen reopens; (#4) TrainerScreen `phaseRef` keeps the `onCommit` subscription stable across phase transitions, removing the rep-by-rep handler churn; (#5) `dispatchCommit(at)` hoisted as a shared callback between the keyboard and phone branches. Three nits APPLIED: (#6) `data-testid=\"input-source-select\"` + `data-testid=\"settings-save\"` plus verify-script switched to testids; (#8) slice's `attachPhonePeer` swap now unwires listeners BEFORE closing the prior peer, with a regression test 'does not broadcast a spurious closed status when swapping peers' that watches `usePhonePeer.subscribe` for any 'closed' status during the swap; (#9) `onCommit` JSDoc clarifies subscribers are global to the slice and survive detach. Findings deferred with rationale: (#7) the 'Phone disconnected ({phoneStatus})' banner can render transitional values — accepted as accurate; downstream phases can refine if it surfaces as confusing in manual QA. Reviewer's optional `@testing-library/react`-based IdleScreen unit test deferred — adding the library is out of scope and the §B2 manual-QA + verify-script gating pattern is the project's established approach for 2b UI flows.",
    "qa_playwright": "Phase 2b.4 DataChannel + motion paths are gated by manual real-device QA per QUALITY_GATES.md §'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b)' — see manual_qa block. Automated UI gate checks C1, C2, C3, C4 in verify-phase-2b4.mjs all PASS with zero console errors; C5 (best-effort Disconnect button visibility) fails under headless chromium without UDP, which is the documented expected outcome — manual M1 covers the peer-outlives-view contract. Phase 4 + Phase 5 + Phase 2b.1 + 2b.2 + 2b.3 regression: not separately re-run this iteration; covered by the full vitest suite (190/190) which gates the analytics + drill + profiles + manual-pairing + QR-pairing + motion modules unchanged in this phase."
  },
  "suggested_commit_message": "phase-2b.4: phone inputSource through Settings/Idle/Trainer + phone-peer slice"
}

